# PATCH: 022-clear-stale-movingtab
#
# Prevents incomplete tab drags from leaving browser chrome inert.
#
# Firefox intentionally disables pointer events for most of the navigation bar
# while the navigator toolbox has the movingtab attribute. Patch 003 permits
# only trusted internal tab transport and routes every blocked drag through
# Firefox's failure cleanup; this patch adds browser-UI defense in depth for
# malformed dataTransfer objects and missing terminal drag events.
#
# Each drag retains its source independently of dataTransfer so malformed drop
# and dragend events can use one cancellation path. The toolbox marker is
# cleared synchronously on drop and dragend, while the tabstrip marker remains
# until any cosmetic same-window translation completes. Normal reorder state,
# including currentIndex, is left intact until Firefox finishes using it.
# The native tab payload keeps Firefox's internal marker with an empty value so
# permitting tab transport cannot disclose the tab URL.
#
# A window-level mouse watchdog can recover even when navbar hit testing is
# disabled or the drag service retained a zombie session. Transitionend and
# transitioncancel handling has a bounded one-second fallback. Firefox's
# navigation-bar drop shielding remains active throughout valid native drags.


